  "version": "0.6.1-beta.4",
  "notes": "## Changes since `v0.6.1-beta.3`\n\n### Features\n\n- manage the SSH key vault in Settings > Security and pick a vault key in the connection dialog, so a key can be imported once, used by any connection on every synced device and exported back to a key file: the private key field of profiles and jump hosts switches between a key file and the key vault and can save a key file into the vault, and the backup, sync and reset texts now say they cover the vault's keys ([cb685ed2](https://github.com/330079598/tTerm/commit/cb685ed25db4c25c863df1b8d7e5b31a0bc1144d))\n- add an SSH key vault that keeps private keys and their certificates encrypted in the database with the saved passwords, so password sync and encrypted backups take them to other devices instead of leaving profiles pointing at key files that only exist on one machine: a profile signs in with a vault key through the private key path tterm-key:<id>, which key loading, automatic authentication, tunnel credential checks and the missing key file report after a restore all resolve, and new commands import, list, rename, re-certify, delete and export keys, the export asking the user to verify it is them ([e5979595](https://github.com/330079598/tTerm/commit/e597959593cc5fb68530849348e5427910fdf204))\n\n**Full comparison:** [v0.6.1-beta.3...v0.6.1-beta.4](https://github.com/330079598/tTerm/compare/v0.6.1-beta.3...v0.6.1-beta.4)",
